WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:28.720
For starshield launches in 43 days from one pad show how quickly the space force is scaling its classified constellation. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 112. SpaceX will fly USSF 385 on a falcon 9 from SLC4E, no earlier than 7AM Pacific Daylight Time Saturday. The mission follows three earlier flights that place 23 satellites each on two of them, and 17 on the third.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:35.760
Booster B110 will make its 10th flight and return to the drone ship, of course I still

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:36.300
love you.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:41.820
The pace reflects heavy space force use of Vandenberg while Cape Infrastructure shifts

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:42.860
towards Starship.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:48.520
Cursor released two new bots that handle security review and deployment monitoring after

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:49.300
code merges.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:56.420
Security reviewer scans each change for injection flaws, broken authentication, committed credentials,

00:00:56.420 --> 00:01:00.420
unsafety serialization and risky dependency updates.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:05.880
It supplies severity ratings, attack path explanations, and one click fixes.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:10.560
Average review time fell from 4.8 minutes to 3.8 minutes,

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.080
and developers now accept the suggestions 60 to 70% of the time.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.760
Rollouts builds a monitoring plan before the merge

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:21.480
and then compares live signals from data dog,

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:25.460
Grafana, or Honeycomb against pre-deployment baselines.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:30.720
When it isolates a genuine regression, it can pause the rollout or open an automated

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.320
revert.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:36.560
Starship Flight 14 completed its wet dress rehearsal successfully this week.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:43.300
Ship 41 was stacked on Booster 21, both stages reached full propellant load, and the count

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:47.420
ran to just before engine ignition before the deluge system activated.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:55.500
ship 41 was then destacked on Friday but stayed at the site. A near-term manifest lists flight 15 no

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:02.820
earlier than October 19th and flight 16 carrying Starlink satellites no earlier than October 30th from

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:12.620
KSC 39A. XAI plans three equal waves of 220,000 GB 300 GPUs that would bring the combined colossus

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:19.300
fleet to 1.44 million accelerators by December. The first wave is expected online within days,

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:24.640
the second in November, and the third by late December if infrastructure targets are met.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.980
NASA added $946 million to its crew contract with SpaceX,

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:36.780
lifting the total value to $5.92 billion across 17 flights through 2030.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:43.680
Crew 13 remains on schedule for this Thursday. Tesla closed its semi-event with a nine-second

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:49.100
roadster clip that showed a SpaceX logo on the trailer doors and a connected front light

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:49.360
bar.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:55.760
Ten Starlink conjunctions currently appear on the Socrates list, yet all carry suspect flags

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.120
from stale tracking data.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:02.780
Seven Starlink satellites carry active reentry predictions as part of routine end-of-life

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:03.340
deorbitant.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:09.840
The Falcon 9 for U.S.S.F. 385 will be the sixth launch from Vandenberg this month.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:14.440
Residents in three nearby counties may hear sonic booms depending on weather.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:20.360
On Reddit, users asked whether Raptor engine bell medals could double as heat shield material,

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.260
given their exposure to higher temperatures than reentry.

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:30.480
Another thread pointed to an FAA presentation that lists Starship Flight 15 for October 19th

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:37.380
flight 16 for Oct. 30. A third post shared official images of ship 41 and

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:41.800
noted the vehicle is now preparing for its first orbital attempt. One thing

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:45.700
worth watching is that power delivery and cooling remain the binding constraints

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:50.860
on the planned colossus expansion. Musk noted the final wave depends on whether

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:55.200
the team gets lucky with infrastructure timelines. The schedule has not been

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:00.500
independently verified. On the AI front, cursors new bots operate after

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:04.880
merges rather than during writing. They compare specific changes against the

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:11.480
full code base and live observability signals. EX AI's three waves of 220,000

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:17.680
GPUs, 300 GPUs, would bring the combined fleet to 1.44 million accelerators by

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:23.500
December if all waves land on schedule. The engineering angle on cursors new bots

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:29.660
centers on shifting verification from human review to automated comparison against live baselines.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:34.680
Security reviewer runs a full code-based scan for each pull request and

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:38.700
surfaces only the categories of flaw that survive ordinary peer review.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:44.580
That produces a measurable drop in review time from 4.8 minutes to 3.8 minutes

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:49.180
while raising acceptance of suggested fixes from 45% to 70%.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:59.180
Rollouts extends the same principle into production by building an instrumentation map before merge and then comparing signals against pre-deployment baselines.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:08.440
When a regression is isolated from an intentional change, the bot can pause the rollout or open a revert pull request before the issue reaches all users.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:14.960
The approach works only when source control, deployment, and observability systems are already connected.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:19.760
Teams lacking that stack face setup overhead that can outweigh the benefit.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:27.240
The design therefore trades broad applicability for depth inside environments that already instrument their services at scale.

